  {"comment": "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT. A fold whose line, carried on past its ends, would pass an earlier fold's seam (mitcad#2226): t = 1, r = 1, crease deduction 2, so each 90 degree crease develops 2 (half a strip h = 1). An L-shaped panel (x 0..140 at the bottom, 0..100 up to y = 100) with a flap A below (x 110..130 down to y = -30) and a flap B on the right of the upper part (y 60..90 out to x = 130), each crease h out from the panel's edge (A at y = -1, B at x = 101), so that past a crease's end the panel lies half a strip back. A folds first; its seam lies at y = 0, x 110..130: past B's near tangent (x = 100) but wholly beside B's line (y 60..90), where B cuts nothing, so B folds and the seam stays on the panel."},
